Strong recommendation for Amazon to stop using EMS!
Commodities five stars, logistics one star, average three stars.
Don't understand why Amazon is sending EMS. Everyone in the industry knows it's unreliable, after all, computers are valuable items!
After the purchase order showed that the number 20 was expected to arrive, so the family waited at home for three days!
Why does it take four to five days to send from Xiamen to Fuzhou?
This morning on the 22nd, I checked the logistics and finally received it in Fuzhou. I was preparing to happily receive the package when, in the evening, without receiving any phone calls or messages, I checked the logistics and found that it had been signed for midday, with even the status showing it as 'personally signed for.'
I was instantly shocked!
Who am I? Where am I? Is this computer really mine?
Isn't it simply suspicious of life?
I finally got my computer back after a trip to the pickup point.
The specific reason, in simple terms, is that the delivery boy mixed up the two tracking numbers, fortunately, the package didn't get lost.
I strongly suggest that Amazon don't use EMS anymore, and I definitely won't buy from them again if they start using EMS for their deliveries.
Awaiting supplier's response
The packaging has no labels and is directly called to the supplier without any identification; they say it's genuine if there's doubt, and can send samples via courier for inspection at Johnson & Johnson Company; they also leave their license plate number and phone number behind, promising to send an SMS notification of my information being inputted into the Johnson & Johnson warranty card; but I haven't received any message yet?
The packaging is damaged, waiting time to check the quality of the product.
The outer packaging is badly damaged, the inner packaging box seems new, but the instructions don't seem new, it's only been repaired in September, in the fridge, hoping it won't be bad by then, please explain to Amazon why many customers mention the packaging is damaged, but you can be safe, thank you!
Things are good, but platform bureaucracy remains.
The hard drive is of excellent quality, has an absolutely high value, is cheaper than Hong Kong, and is absolutely recommended for purchase if it is not in a hurry and can tolerate logistics.
But it has to be said that Amazon’s bureaucracy remains, unchanged from years ago when I swore I would never use it again, and you can never track the actual shipping status, information is always delivered weeks later, and you can never complain, that's so bureaucratic!
It has been days since the shipment arrived, but the logistics information still shows that you will receive the goods 10 days from now!
